# CLAUDE RULES & AGENT SHIELD POLICIES — BOXTOOLS (PEVC V5)

## 1. Zero Docker Rule for Databases
- Under NO circumstances shall `supabase start` or local Docker containers be required for database operations.
- All DDL/DML, migrations and schema inspections MUST be performed against Supabase Cloud via the official MCP server or remote HTTPS API.

## 2. Visual-First Verification Barrier
- Product and business logic code shall NEVER be considered ready for merge without visual inspection.
- Every UI surface MUST be tested across 1440px (Desktop), 768px (Tablet), and 375px (Mobile).
- Horizontal overflow (`scrollWidth > clientWidth`) is strictly forbidden.

## 3. Strict TDD Flow (Red ➔ Green ➔ Blue)
- Every user-facing feature must be accompanied by automated E2E tests (Playwright) verifying both state transitions and visual stability.

## 4. Secret & Token Isolation (AgentShield)
- `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, and AI Provider keys (Gemini, OpenAI) must never be committed to source control or exposed in client bundles.
- All sensitive credentials must remain in `.env.local` or encrypted in `ai_settings` with strict RLS (`auth.uid() = user_id`).
